claims.statement:
Bad-class certificate soundness (general). Let C be a strip certificate for word w and width b (ranks rk, positions ps, periods m, words u, as in newideas Cert), and let `bad` be a rank. Suppose:
- along every edge (phase, s) -> (phase+1, lin3(w(phase) :: s ++ [x])) the rank does not increase;
- along rank-preserving edges in every class other than `bad`, the position advances like a counter mod m(r) at white phases and column 1 equals u(r, pos);
- checkGb holds for every class other than `bad`.
If cell t 0 = w((t-T) mod P) for all t >= T, then there is T' >= T with rk((t-T) mod P, rowR t b) = bad for all t >= T'. Any Boolean predicate that holds on every node of the bad class therefore holds eventually along the true history (Cert.eventually_pred).

Skeleton for 0011. If cell t 0 = decide(2 <= (t-T) % 4) for all t >= T, then there is T' >= T such that for all t >= T':
- phase 0: cell t (-1) = cell t 1;
- phase 1: cell t 1 = true and cell t (-1) = false;
- phase 2: cell t 1 = true and cell t (-1) = false;
- phase 3: cell t 1 = false and cell t (-1) = true.

Skeleton for 0001. If cell t 0 = decide((t-T) % 4 = 3) for all t >= T, then there is T' >= T such that for all t >= T':
- phase 0: cell t 1 = false, cell t 3 = true, cell t (-1) = false;
- phase 1: cell t 2 = true and cell t (-1) = cell t 1;
- phase 2: cell t 1 = true and cell t (-1) = false;
- phase 3: cell t 1 = true, cell t 2 = false, cell t (-1) = true.
So column 1 is (0, y, 1, 1) and column -1 is (0, y, 0, 1) with the same free bit y_k = cell(T+4k+1, 1).

None of the following is monotone along constrained histories (all 2.1M surviving two-step transitions from starts of width <= 22). The change per two steps ranged over:
- weight [-16, 11];
- walls (equal adjacent pairs) [-10, 14]; 00-walls [-11, 17]; 11-walls [-17, 14];
- class-1 walls (k+t odd) [-10, 9]; class-0 walls [-10, 9];
- first deviation from the stripe [-2, 19] (decreases by exactly 2 per epoch step, jumps at resets);
- number of deviations [-11, 14]; runs of ones [-6, 6];
- weight at odd depths [-9, 8] and at even depths [-9, 8];
- position of the first class-1 wall [-24, 24];
- parity of the wall count in the cone (flips every step whatever the constraint).
Also: no ZBL row other than the stripe is a fixed point satisfying the constraint, and the 00-pair parity identity along anti-diagonals carries no sign.

established:
[Lean] ZBL structure (R30ProgA):
- backward determinism at forced steps and an exact finite-preimage criterion (backward_det, back_fin_iff);
- forced skeleton: the next forced step survives iff cells -2 and -3 differ (survive_iff); columns -1 and -2 are never both white (no_two_white);
- light cone, pivot and zero-run localization;
- edge-region barrier (edge_region_barrier): any far part can be completed near the wall so that column -1 takes any prescribed values before time d, while the far region's evolution is unchanged. Consequently, left-edge structure combined with the constraint on a window shorter than the wall-to-structure distance proves nothing.

[Refuted by exact computation] Beyond depth about 15, the map f ↦ Phi(f) has no low-complexity structure:
- the only affine identities among 1, L(1..33) are L1=1, L2+L3=1 and L2+L5=1;
- Nullstellensatz certificate degree grows with K;
- no finite transducer exists (Myhill–Nerode classes grow ≈1.79^s);
- no self-similarity under any of 10 transforms;
- no GF(2)-affine invariant;
- no wall-reading DFA ranking with ≤ 6 states (z3 UNSAT);
- no simple monovariant (weight, wall counts, deviations and others) over 2.1M surviving transitions;
- minimal forced windows grow ≈0.8a, so bounded-window identity families cannot work.

[Synthesis check] The ether underlies both programs (checked in synth-r2/ether_check.py). JointBarrier's c7 = (1000000)^∞ is exactly the 7×4 ether, shifted by 4 in space and 0 in time. Its center column B4 = 0101 alternates. Its left half evolves exactly as the ZBL with a white wall, column -1 is black at every black time, and the free bits alternate: f = (10)^∞ = ¬(column 1 at white times). So the ether is an infinite two-sided configuration that satisfies every period-2 constraint. It is simultaneously:
- Phi((10)^∞), the period-7 member of the constrained set;
- the background of the period-4 traps;
- the witness family of the two-sided barrier.
